        "char_end": 478,
        "char_start": 310,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 155,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 156,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Use the trigonometric identity for cosine of supplementary angles.\n\\[\n\\cos(180^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPS = -\\cos \\angle RPQ\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 853,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 854,
        "char_start": 480,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 353,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 354,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Determine \\(\\cos \\angle RPQ\\).\nSince \\(\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1\\),\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{7}{25}\\right)^2 + \\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{49}{625} + \\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = 1 - \\frac{49}{625}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = \\frac{625}{625} - \\frac{49}{625}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = \\frac{576}{625}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPQ = \\pm \\frac{24}{25}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1098,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1099,
        "char_start": 856,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 431,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 432,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Since \\(\\angle RPQ\\) is an angle in a right triangle where the opposite side to \\(\\angle RPQ\\) is shorter than the adjacent side, \\(\\angle RPQ\\) must be acute, thus \\(\\cos \\angle RPQ\\) is positive.\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPQ = \\frac{24}{25}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1197,
