  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the given information and the goal.\nGiven: \\(\\sin \\angle RPQ = \\frac{7}{25}\\).\nGoal: Find \\(\\cos \\angle RPS\\).\n\nStep 2: Recognize that \\(\\angle RPQ\\) and \\(\\angle RPS\\) are supplementary angles because they form a straight line at point P.\nTherefore, \\(\\angle RPS = 180^\\circ - \\angle RPQ\\).\n\nStep 3: Use the trigonometric identity for cosine of supplementary angles.\n\\[\n\\cos(180^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPS = -\\cos \\angle RPQ\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Determine \\(\\cos \\angle RPQ\\).\nSince \\(\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1\\),\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{7}{25}\\right)^2 + \\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{49}{625} + \\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = 1 - \\frac{49}{625}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = \\frac{625}{625} - \\frac{49}{625}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos^2 \\angle RPQ = \\frac{576}{625}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPQ = \\pm \\frac{24}{25}\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Since \\(\\angle RPQ\\) is an angle in a right triangle where the opposite side to \\(\\angle RPQ\\) is shorter than the adjacent side, \\(\\angle RPQ\\) must be acute, thus \\(\\cos \\angle RPQ\\) is positive.\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPQ = \\frac{24}{25}\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Apply the identity from Step 3.\n\\[\n\\cos \\angle RPS = -\\cos \\angle RPQ = -\\frac{24}{25}\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-\\frac{24}{25}}<|im_end|>",
